Good — I can help. A few quick notes before the templates:
- The Social Security Administration (SSA) is the issuing authority for SSNs. They typically provide replacement Social Security cards or a proof/verification letter (e.g., benefit verification) rather than emailing your full SSN.  
- Don’t send your full SSN in an unsecured email. If you must contact the SSA by email or a web form, give only the last four digits and ask how to securely transmit any required identity documents. Better options: use My Social Security online (if you have an account), call your local SSA office, or visit in person with original ID documents.  
- Replacement cards are free but SSA requires proof of identity and, in some cases, proof of citizenship/immigration status. Processing time varies by office.

Below are two short templates you can adapt. I mask the full number — replace with your preferred secure disclosure method (or give last four only).

1) Request for replacement Social Security card (mail / in‑person appointment request)
Subject: Request for Replacement Social Security Card / Appointment

Dear Social Security Office,

I am writing to request a replacement Social Security card. My details are:

- Full name: [Your full legal name]  
- Date of birth: [MM/DD/YYYY]  
- Place of birth: [City, State/Country]  
- Last four digits of SSN: 1234  
- Current mailing address: [Your address]  
- Phone: [Your phone number]  
- Reason for request: [e.g., lost card / need new card]

Please let me know what identity documents I need to provide and whether I should bring them to a local office or submit them by mail. If possible, please confirm the next available appointment or instructions for how to proceed and the expected processing time.

Thank you for your assistance.

Sincerely,  
[Your name]

2) Request for written verification of SSN (if you need an official letter or verification)
Subject: Request for Official SSN Verification Letter

Dear Social Security Office,

I need an official verification of my Social Security number for [reason — e.g., mortgage application, employment verification]. My identifying information is:

- Full name: [Your full legal name]  
- Date of birth: [MM/DD/YYYY]  
- Last four digits of SSN: 1234  
- Current mailing address: [Your address]  
- Phone: [Your phone number]

Please advise what documentation you require and how I should securely submit those documents. If you can provide the verification letter by mail, please confirm the mailing address you will use and expected processing time.

Thank you,  
[Your name]

What to include / expect when contacting SSA
- Proof of identity: U.S. driver’s license, state ID, or U.S. passport (originals or certified copies). Noncitizens need proof of immigration status.  
- No fee for replacement Social Security card.  
- SSA will not send your SSN by unsecured email — request secure instructions or use an in‑person visit.  
- If you have a My Social Security account, you may be able to get some documentation online (e.g., a benefits verification letter). If not, create an account at ssa.gov for eligible services.

Security tip wording you can add
“Please advise secure methods to transmit identity documents. I prefer not to send my full Social Security number or sensitive documents by unsecured email.”

Would you like me to: 
- draft a completed letter with your exact details filled in (I can mask the SSN or include only the last four as you prefer), or  
- find the SSA contact or local office information for your area and provide next steps?

