[Your current address]
[City, State ZIP]
[Phone number]
[Email address]
[Date]

Social Security Administration
[Local office address or “Office of the Commissioner” if mailing nationally]

Re: Request for replacement Social Security card / verification of SSN (SSN ending in 1234)

Dear Sir or Madam,

I am writing to request a copy of my Social Security card (or an official verification letter of my Social Security number). My Social Security number ends in 1234. For your records, my identifying information is:

- Full name: [Your full legal name]
- Date of birth: [MM/DD/YYYY]
- Place of birth: [City, State/Country]
- Mother’s maiden name (if required): [Name]
- Current address: [Your address]

I have enclosed/attached copies of the required identity documents: [list — e.g., U.S. passport / state driver’s license / certified birth certificate]. Please advise if you require any additional documents or forms. If you prefer, I can appear in person at my local SSA office to complete any necessary paperwork.

Please send the replacement card (or verification letter) to the above address, or contact me at [phone] or [email] to arrange delivery or pickup.

Thank you for your assistance.

Sincerely,
[Your name]
[Signature if mailing]

2) Short email template (to an official, secure SSA email/contact form)
Subject: Request for replacement SSN card / verification — SSN ending in 1234

Hello,

I would like to request a replacement Social Security card (or an official verification letter for my SSN). My SSN ends in 1234. My name is [Your full name], DOB [MM/DD/YYYY]. I can provide identity documents (driver’s license/passport) and complete any required forms.

Please let me know the next steps, required documents, and whether I should apply online, mail documents, or visit my local SSA office.

Thank you,
