Short checklist to prepare before contacting the SSA
- Have an acceptable ID ready (e.g., U.S. passport, state driver’s license). The SSA will tell you which originals they need.
- Know your full legal name, date of birth, place of birth, and current mailing address.
- If you need a replacement card, be ready to complete the SSA replacement-card form (SS-5) or use the SSA online portal if eligible.
- Prefer secure channels: SSA website/online account, local SSA office in person, or their official phone number — avoid sending full SSN in unsecured email.

