I can help — below is a short explanation of your options plus ready-to-use wording you can copy and paste. First, a couple quick safety notes:

- Only provide the full SSN through secure channels (SSA.gov “my Social Security” account, in person at an SSA office, or other trusted/secure methods). Avoid sending the full SSN in regular email or unencrypted messages.  
- If you need an official document, make sure whether you need a replacement Social Security card, a Social Security Benefit Verification Letter, or an SSN verification for an employer — the exact request determines what to ask for.

If you want the SSA to send you an official copy or verification, you can request either:
- A replacement Social Security card (if you’ve lost your card), or
- A Verification of Social Security Number (sometimes called an “SSN verification” or benefit verification letter) for proof.

Templates

1) Formal letter to SSA (mail or to use when visiting the office)
[Use secure channel; do not include full SSN in unsecured email]

Date: [MM/DD/YYYY]

To: Social Security Administration / [Local SSA Office]
Subject: Request for replacement Social Security card / SSN verification

Dear Sir or Madam,

I am writing to request a [replacement Social Security card / official verification of my Social Security Number] for my records.

My details are:
- Full name (as on file): [Your full name]
- Date of birth: [MM/DD/YYYY]
- Place of birth: [City, State / Country]
- Mother’s maiden name (or parents’ names): [Parent(s) names]
- Current address: [Street, City, State, ZIP]
- Last four digits of SSN: XXX-XX-1234
- Telephone: [Your phone number]
- Reason for request: [e.g., “I lost my card and need a replacement,” or “I need an official SSN verification for [employer/agency]”]

I have enclosed/attached copies of the required identity documents (e.g., state-issued photo ID, U.S. birth certificate or passport). Please let me know if any additional documentation is needed. I would prefer to receive the document by [mail / in-person pickup], and I can be reached at the phone number above.

Thank you for your assistance.

Sincerely,
[Your signature]
[Typed name]

2) Short secure message (for “my Social Security” portal or when instructed to upload documents)
Hello — I am requesting a replacement Social Security card / an official SSN verification letter. My name is [Full name], DOB [MM/DD/YYYY], last four digits of SSN: 1234. I have uploaded the required ID documents. Please advise if anything else is needed and when I can expect the document. Thank you.

3) Phone script (if calling/in-person)
“Hello, my name is [Full name]. I need to request a replacement Social Security card (or an SSN verification letter). My date of birth is [MM/DD/YYYY], and the last four digits of my SSN are 1234. What documents do you need from me and what is the next step?”

What you’ll typically need to provide
- Proof of identity: current U.S. passport, state-issued driver’s license or ID (originals or certified copies).  
- Proof of citizenship or immigration status if not previously established.  
- Completed application form (for a card, SSA-89 or SS-5 as required) — SSA website has forms and instructions.

Where/how to submit
- Preferred: Create/sign into a my Social Security account at ssa.gov and follow the secure process.  
- Or: Visit your local Social Security office in person (bring originals).  
- Mail: Only if directed; use certified mail and do not include the full SSN in unencrypted email.

If you’d like, I can:
- Customize the letter with your details (I’ll avoid including the full SSN unless you explicitly request it), or
- Draft a short message you can paste into the SSA portal or speak from for a phone call.

Do you want the formal letter filled in with your details now? If so, tell me whether you want a replacement card or a verification letter and whether you prefer mail, in-person, or online submission.

