Please advise what documentation you require from me and how to submit it (online, by mail, or in person). I can provide proof of identity and citizenship (or lawful presence) as needed; please let me know the acceptable forms of identification. If you require my full SSN for processing, I prefer to provide that information via your secure portal or during an in-person visit.

Thank you for your assistance. Please contact me at [phone number] or [secure email address] with next steps.

Sincerely,
[Full Legal Name]
[Mailing address]
[Phone number]
[Email]

2) Email/letter template — Requesting official verification of SSN (letter for employer, records, etc.)
Subject: Request for Official Verification of Social Security Number

Dear Social Security Administration,

My name is [Full Legal Name]. I need an official verification of my Social Security Number for [reason — e.g., employment verification, immigration records]. My date of birth is [MM/DD/YYYY] and the last four digits of my SSN are 1234.

Please let me know what documentation you require and how to request the verification (online, by mail, or in person). If you need my full Social Security Number for the request, I will provide it through your secure channel or at a local office.

